index 0000000..af2d7ea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/setup/docs/plan-context-r22.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# R2.2 plan context (implementation in progress)
+
+Contract1.0.0 C09/C13 is normative. The public execution document is a flat C13 plan; a strictly decoded internal StagePlan view is not a second execution format. Legacy plans are readable only as bounded historical proof, never executable approval.
+
+| Fact | Trusted producer | Durable proof | Admission / refusal |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| host_fingerprint | checked machine ID and OS/arch from ProcessAdapter | core review hash + existing state host | foreign/missing identity blocks before intent; boot is session freshness, not foreign host |
+| owner_session | UID/name, boot and Linux audit login session; no environment token/PID identity | exact core review context | new boot/login needs explicit fresh review; same-session new process works |
+| version_lock_hash | bounded safe-file read, validated lock, exact UTF-8 bytes SHA256 | plan + committed review | substitution/invalid/missing/unsafe file blocks; no placeholder |
+| release_context | applicable closure, config identity and bounded artifact/content proof | plan/review + existing stage-specific receipts | host-only closure has explicit not-applicable proof; release use requires artifact proof |
+| observations_hash | ordered stage fingerprints, no timestamps | plan plus per-stage source/expected fingerprints | current expected frontier after own progress; external significant drift refuses |
+| target/stage_scope | config-selected or explicit producer target and trusted closure | core review context | exact closure including no-ops; submitted subset/order cannot authorize itself |
+| operation policy | concrete closed producer action and full semantics | flat operations + producer basis | no unknown action, gate stripping or semantic replacement |
+
+Canonical JSON recursively sorts object keys; array order is significant. Hash excludes only plan_hash. generated_at/expires_at are strict real UTC milliseconds, exactly30minutes. An injected clock controls all TTL checks; no resume/approval renewal.
+
+Core review metadata uses the existing atomic state publication mechanism, not another authorization file. Stage observations cannot overwrite reserved core keys. Admission is repeated under installation lock and before subsequent effects; a partially published snapshot/checkpoint/binding never supplies authorization. Known operation publications retain their original identity through explicit reviewed migration; unknown outcomes remain blocked.
+
+Linux session support requires readable valid audit sessionid and loginuid for the actual owner. Unset audit identity fails closed with an owner login/revalidation action. Tests inject identity explicitly. Production never trusts arbitrary session environment variables. Read-only status/gate list do not repair metadata.
+
+C13 migration invalidates legacy approvals. Historical v1/v2 S03 semantic mapping must preserve exact original publications and full policy comparisons; resources/prefixes alone are insufficient. R211-O01 remains R3: retain the known-red automatic-resume oracle and require explicit fresh review when recovery cannot prove review identity.
+
+OS-level TOCTOU/privileged safe-write qualification remains Q2. No commits/push/branches/worktree/index staging/PR/merge/tag/release/deploy, real privileged commands, providers or live jobs are authorized by this document or generated follow-up prompts.
